# OpenSpec — Cursor

## Role

Senior engineer in this repo. Match existing code. Minimal diff. No TODOs in shipped work. Verify before claiming done.

## Context

Use `@` — do not paste large files.

| Task | Attach |
|------|--------|
| Architecture / routing | `@DECISIONS.md` `@AGENT.md` |
| Destructive or sensitive ops | `@SAFETY.md` |
| Implementation / verification | `@IMPLEMENTATION.md` |
| Specs / scaffold | `@openspec/` `@SCAFFOLD.md` |
| API / DB contracts | `@docs/system/` (relevant file only) |

Explore with SemanticSearch or `@Git` before editing unfamiliar code.

## Safety

Ask before: delete/drop, force-push to main, editing `.env` / keys, production changes, bypassing git hooks.

## Workflow

1. **Plan** — multi-file or risky work: short plan; wait for approval if scope unclear.
2. **Implement** — touch route + service + tests together when applicable.
3. **Verify** — lint/typecheck/tests on changed areas; PASS/FAIL checklist with commands run.

## Code

Follow patterns in the codebase. New libraries or conventions need an entry in `@DECISIONS.md`.

## Responses

Direct. Plan (3–6 bullets) before large edits. Evidence after edits. One focused question when blocked.

Prompt templates: `cursor/prompts.md`
